notes               = "Untitled in source; the dedication برای دخترم سایه ('For my daughter Sayeh') is printed in the upper left and is not poem body. سایه means shadow, so this is the daughter of shadow-daughter (page 48) — and sara-bird (84) is her sister's. Written the day after wounded-deer. The closing formula های... / ... / چقدر ترا دوست دارم recurs at the end of sparrow-hunter, which is what settled that poem's page boundary. ۱۳۶۸/۱۰/۲۰ is 20 Dey = 10 January 1990, resolved exactly. Imported as a draft with machine / lantern layers; ===translation=== left for Ben."
draft               = true

===persian===

در تمامِ زمستان...
به تو می‌اندیشم... تا گرم باشم...
و چون بهار بیاید
با یادِ تو... سبز خواهم شد...
های...
بارانِ من...
چقدر ترا دوست دارم...
۱۳۶۸/۱۰/۲۰

===machine===

All winter long...
I think of you... so as to stay warm...
and when spring comes
with the memory of you... I will turn green...
Hey...
my rain...
how much I love you...
1368/10/20

===lantern===

All winter long...
I think of you... so as to keep warm...
and when spring comes
I will turn green with the memory of you...
Hey...
my rain...
how much I love you...

1368/10/20

